@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@
+---
+paths:
+  - "src/test/java/**/*.java"
+---
+# Tests
+
+Contents: 1. Substitutes and test data named for their work
+
+## 1. Substitutes and test data named for their work
+
+Name a substitute that you write by hand and that keeps its data in memory with the port it stands for and then InMemory, such as ReminderSenderInMemory. Name a class that builds test data with the concept and then Factory, such as LoanFactory. A reader of a test then knows from the name alone whether a class stands in for a port or only builds the data of a test.
diff --git a/.claude/rules/conventions/web.md b/.claude/rules/conventions/web.md
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/.claude/rules/conventions/web.md
@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@
+---
+paths:
+  - "src/main/java/**/in/web/**/*.java"
+---
+# Web entry
+
+Contents: 1. The classes at the root of in/web
+
+## 1. The classes at the root of in/web
+
+Keep at the root of the in/web folder of a module only the classes that the folder exists for, and name each with its concept first: a controller ends in RestController, such as LoanRestController, and an exception handler ends in WebExceptionHandler, such as LoanWebExceptionHandler. Put their helpers into subfolders named for their kind, such as response for the types of a call and converter for the classes that build them. A reader sees at the root which calls the module answers, and the last word of each class tells the entry it serves.
+
+- Limits: belonging, not a count of files, decides where a helper goes.
